{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JWdfjZQmokARa4HNrL3J8w","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"RMS acceleration velocity blast vibration pore pressure cyclic shear strain threshold\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Frontiers | Cyclic threshold shear strain for pore water pressure generation and stiffness degradation in marine clays at Yangtze estuary\",\"url\":\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2023.1184225/full\"},{\"title\":\"Cyclic threshold shear strain in pore water pressure generation in clay in situ samples - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0038080618300684\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Cyclic Shear Strain Needed for Liquefaction Triggering and Assessment of Overburden Pressure Factor Kσ\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/279239866_Cyclic_Shear_Strain_Needed_for_Liquefaction_Triggering_and_Assessment_of_Overburden_Pressure_Factor_Ks\"},{\"title\":\"Threshold Shear Strain for Cyclic Pore-Water Pressure in Cohesive Soils | Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering | Vol 132, No 10\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/%28ASCE%291090-0241%282006%29132%3A10%281325%29\"},{\"title\":\"13th World Conference on Earthquake Engineering Vancouver, B.C., Canada\",\"url\":\"https://www.iitk.ac.in/nicee/wcee/article/13_2580.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Threshold Shear Strain for Cyclic Pore-Water Pressure in ...\",\"url\":\"http://ascelibrary.org/doi/abs/10.1061/(ASCE)1090-0241(2006)132:10(1325)\"},{\"title\":\"Cyclic threshold strains in clays versus sands and the change of secant shear modulus and pore water pressure at small cyclic strains\",\"url\":\"https://escholarship.org/uc/item/9gw5h5xc\"},{\"title\":\"1 CYCLIC TRIAXIAL TEST TO MEASURE STRAIN-DEPENDENT SHEAR 1\",\"url\":\"https://par.nsf.gov/servlets/purl/10478063\"}]\n\nI found relevant research on this topic. Here's what the search results reveal:\n\n## Cyclic Threshold Shear Strain and Pore Pressure\n\nThreshold shear strain for cyclic pore-water pressure is a fundamental property of fully saturated soils subjected to undrained cyclic loading. At cyclic shear strain amplitudes larger than this threshold, residual cyclic pore-water pressure changes rapidly.\n\n## Threshold Values\n\nThe threshold values vary depending on soil type:\n- For clay in situ samples, the initial threshold shear strain to initiate soil nonlinearity ranged from 0.002% to 0.003%, and to trigger generation of residual excess pore pressures ranged from 0.008% to 0.012%.\n- In sands, the threshold shear strain is approximately 0.01%, measured by many researchers over a 40-year period and is remarkably constant.\n\n## Blast-Induced Response\n\nControlled blasting can be used as a source of seismic energy to characterize dynamic response, where shear strain and corresponding residual excess pore pressures are associated with low-frequency near- and far-field shear waves within earthquake frequency ranges.\n\n## Post-Straining Effects\n\nFollowing pre-straining and dissipation of excess pore pressures, the shear strain necessary to trigger residual excess pore pressure increased two-fold.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d52a3ef-833c-4d3d-a19f-380d6d5297be","uuid":"cd5840a1-3e98-449d-8860-1c6630e4a053","timestamp":"2026-07-06T17:11:47.459Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"RMS acceleration velocity blast vibration pore pressure cyclic shear strain threshold","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01BVE5QAzfkExp1kL98r3Nor","content":[{"title":"Frontiers | Cyclic threshold shear strain for pore water pressure generation and stiffness degradation in marine clays at Yangtze estuary","url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2023.1184225/full"},{"title":"Cyclic threshold shear strain in pore water pressure generation in clay in situ samples - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0038080618300684"},{"title":"(PDF) Cyclic Shear Strain Needed for Liquefaction Triggering and Assessment of Overburden Pressure Factor Kσ","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/279239866_Cyclic_Shear_Strain_Needed_for_Liquefaction_Triggering_and_Assessment_of_Overburden_Pressure_Factor_Ks"},{"title":"Threshold Shear Strain for Cyclic Pore-Water Pressure in Cohesive Soils | Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering | Vol 132, No 10","url":"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/%28ASCE%291090-0241%282006%29132%3A10%281325%29"},{"title":"13th World Conference on Earthquake Engineering Vancouver, B.C., Canada","url":"https://www.iitk.ac.in/nicee/wcee/article/13_2580.pdf"},{"title":"Threshold Shear Strain for Cyclic Pore-Water Pressure in ...","url":"http://ascelibrary.org/doi/abs/10.1061/(ASCE)1090-0241(2006)132:10(1325)"},{"title":"Cyclic threshold strains in clays versus sands and the change of secant shear modulus and pore water pressure at small cyclic strains","url":"https://escholarship.org/uc/item/9gw5h5xc"},{"title":"1 CYCLIC TRIAXIAL TEST TO MEASURE STRAIN-DEPENDENT SHEAR 1","url":"https://par.nsf.gov/servlets/purl/10478063"}]},"I found relevant research on this topic. Here's what the search results reveal:\n\n## Cyclic Threshold Shear Strain and Pore Pressure\n\nThreshold shear strain for cyclic pore-water pressure is a fundamental property of fully saturated soils subjected to undrained cyclic loading. At cyclic shear strain amplitudes larger than this threshold, residual cyclic pore-water pressure changes rapidly.\n\n## Threshold Values\n\nThe threshold values vary depending on soil type:\n- For clay in situ samples, the initial threshold shear strain to initiate soil nonlinearity ranged from 0.002% to 0.003%, and to trigger generation of residual excess pore pressures ranged from 0.008% to 0.012%.\n- In sands, the threshold shear strain is approximately 0.01%, measured by many researchers over a 40-year period and is remarkably constant.\n\n## Blast-Induced Response\n\nControlled blasting can be used as a source of seismic energy to characterize dynamic response, where shear strain and corresponding residual excess pore pressures are associated with low-frequency near- and far-field shear waves within earthquake frequency ranges.\n\n## Post-Straining Effects\n\nFollowing pre-straining and dissipation of excess pore pressures, the shear strain necessary to trigger residual excess pore pressure increased two-fold."],"durationSeconds":11.563452833999996,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017LEGDJxjEyD4pfG1EspZr5","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"response spectra PGA PGV blast vibration geotechnical limitation tailings weakly supported\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Estimation of Peak Ground-motion Parameters from ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/pdf/10.1080/13632460601123156\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Ground Motion Model for the Vertical-to-Horizontal (V/H) Ratios of PGA, PGV, and Response Spectra\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/290229590_Ground_Motion_Model_for_the_Vertical-to-Horizontal_VH_Ratios_of_PGA_PGV_and_Response_Spectra\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Vertical ground motion model for PGA, PGV, and linear response spectra using the NGA-West2 database\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/276114266_Vertical_ground_motion_model_for_PGA_PGV_and_linear_response_spectra_using_the_NGA-West2_database\"},{\"title\":\"Ground Motion Model for the Vertical-to-Horizontal (V/H) Ratios of PGA, PGV, and Response Spectra - Yousef Bozorgnia, Kenneth W. Campbell, 2016\",\"url\":\"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1193/100614eqs151m\"},{\"title\":\"Full article: The Estimation of Peak Ground-motion Parameters from Spectral Ordinates\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/13632460601123156\"},{\"title\":\"Earthquake Hazards 201 - Technical Q&A | U.S. Geological Survey\",\"url\":\"https://www.usgs.gov/programs/earthquake-hazards/science/earthquake-hazards-201-technical-qa\"},{\"title\":\"A Non-ergodic Spectral Acceleration Ground Motion Model for California   Developed with Random Vibration Theory\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2107.09125\"}]\n\nI've performed the web search for your query about response spectra, PGA, PGV, blast vibration, geotechnical limitations, and tailings. The search results returned relevant academic sources on ground motion modeling and response spectral analysis.\n\nThe results include:\n\n1. **Spectral Ordinates and Peak Ground Motion Parameters**: Relationships are derived between peak ground-motion parameters and the peaks in the corresponding 5% damped response spectrum.\n\n2. **PGV as a Geotechnical Indicator**: PGV appears to be one of the best single predictors of structural damage and geotechnical effects.\n\n3. **Applications**: Relationships between spectral ordinates and PGV are useful for estimating PGV from a smoothed design spectrum for uses including estimation of structural damage and geotechnical effects.\n\n4. **Vertical Ground Motion Models**: Several sources discuss comprehensive ground motion models (GMM) for vertical components of PGA and PGV using extensive earthquake databases.\n\nHowever, the search results focused primarily on earthquake-related ground motion modeling rather than blast vibration effects on tailings or weakly supported structures. For more specific information about blast-induced vibrations and their geotechnical limitations for tailings facilities, you may need to conduct additional searches with more specific terminology related to mining or blast engineering.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d52a3ef-833c-4d3d-a19f-380d6d5297be","uuid":"971ec9b8-880d-415e-be25-ff9c12ae83e2","timestamp":"2026-07-06T17:11:47.599Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"response spectra PGA PGV blast vibration geotechnical limitation tailings weakly supported","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Cszr4uVudHsVwCHHQrSPA5","content":[{"title":"The Estimation of Peak Ground-motion Parameters from ...","url":"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/pdf/10.1080/13632460601123156"},{"title":"(PDF) Ground Motion Model for the Vertical-to-Horizontal (V/H) Ratios of PGA, PGV, and Response Spectra","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/290229590_Ground_Motion_Model_for_the_Vertical-to-Horizontal_VH_Ratios_of_PGA_PGV_and_Response_Spectra"},{"title":"(PDF) Vertical ground motion model for PGA, PGV, and linear response spectra using the NGA-West2 database","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/276114266_Vertical_ground_motion_model_for_PGA_PGV_and_linear_response_spectra_using_the_NGA-West2_database"},{"title":"Ground Motion Model for the Vertical-to-Horizontal (V/H) Ratios of PGA, PGV, and Response Spectra - Yousef Bozorgnia, Kenneth W. Campbell, 2016","url":"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1193/100614eqs151m"},{"title":"Full article: The Estimation of Peak Ground-motion Parameters from Spectral Ordinates","url":"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/13632460601123156"},{"title":"Earthquake Hazards 201 - Technical Q&A | U.S. Geological Survey","url":"https://www.usgs.gov/programs/earthquake-hazards/science/earthquake-hazards-201-technical-qa"},{"title":"A Non-ergodic Spectral Acceleration Ground Motion Model for California   Developed with Random Vibration Theory","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2107.09125"}]},"I've performed the web search for your query about response spectra, PGA, PGV, blast vibration, geotechnical limitations, and tailings. The search results returned relevant academic sources on ground motion modeling and response spectral analysis.\n\nThe results include:\n\n1. **Spectral Ordinates and Peak Ground Motion Parameters**: Relationships are derived between peak ground-motion parameters and the peaks in the corresponding 5% damped response spectrum.\n\n2. **PGV as a Geotechnical Indicator**: PGV appears to be one of the best single predictors of structural damage and geotechnical effects.\n\n3. **Applications**: Relationships between spectral ordinates and PGV are useful for estimating PGV from a smoothed design spectrum for uses including estimation of structural damage and geotechnical effects.\n\n4. **Vertical Ground Motion Models**: Several sources discuss comprehensive ground motion models (GMM) for vertical components of PGA and PGV using extensive earthquake databases.\n\nHowever, the search results focused primarily on earthquake-related ground motion modeling rather than blast vibration effects on tailings or weakly supported structures. For more specific information about blast-induced vibrations and their geotechnical limitations for tailings facilities, you may need to conduct additional searches with more specific terminology related to mining or blast engineering."],"durationSeconds":10.121747208999993,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013KQYuEgHbXDYgbjU9SJHtZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CAV pore water pressure sandy soil correlation intensity measure Baziar Shahnazari\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Correlations between Pore Pressure Development in Sandy Soil and 62 Ground Motion Intensity Measures by Chi-Chin Tsai, Jui-Pin Wang, Tsai-Yu Huang, Chia-Ying Sung :: SSRN\",\"url\":\"https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4010372\"},{\"title\":\"Correlations between pore water pressure development in sandy soil and CAV-based ground motion intensity measures - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0013795222002708\"},{\"title\":\"Key factors affecting prediction of seismic pore water pressures in silty sands based on damage parameter | Bulletin of Earthquake Engineering | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10518-018-0411-z\"},{\"title\":\"A simple procedure to calibrate a pore pressure energy-based model from in situ tests | Acta Geotechnica | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11440-022-01650-1\"},{\"title\":\"Seismic Sliding Analysis of Sandy Slopes Subjected to Pore-Water Pressure Buildup | International Journal of Geomechanics | Vol 17, No 11\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/abs/10.1061/(ASCE)GM.1943-5622.0001013\"},{\"title\":\"Stress-based evaluation of pore pressure generation in sands subjected to undrained cyclic loading - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1674775526001599\"},{\"title\":\"Excess pore water pressure generation in saturated sandy soils subjected to various cyclic stress paths - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726123000490\"},{\"title\":\"Prediction of Excess Pore Water Pressure Generation in Sand–Silt Mixtures During Cyclic Loading: A Dissipated Energy-Based Model | Geotechnical and Geological Engineering | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10706-024-02837-x\"},{\"title\":\"Pore Water Pressure Generation and Energy Dissipation Characteristics of Sand–Gravel Mixtures Subjected to Cyclic Loading\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2673-7094/4/4/65\"},{\"title\":\"Rapid consolidation and compaction method for soil improvement of various layers of soils and intermediate geomaterials in a soil deposit\",\"url\":\"https://image-ppubs.uspto.gov/dirsearch-public/print/downloadPdf/11124937\"}]\n\nThe search has returned relevant results focusing on the correlation between pore water pressure (PWP) development in sandy soils and various ground motion intensity measures, including CAV (cumulative absolute velocity).\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**CAV and Pore Water Pressure Correlation:**\nCutoff cumulative absolute velocities (CAV) with cutoff acceleration of 0.02~0.04 g are well correlated with PWP development in sandy soil, better than the original CAV without cutoff acceleration. PGA has a weak correlation with PWP development among the 62 intensity measures investigated, ranked 61st.\n\n**Baziar and Shahnazari's Research:**\nBaziar and Shahnazari conducted a laboratory study on the pore pressure generation model for Firouzkooh silty sands using hollow torsional test. Their research has focused on pore pressure generation in sandy and silty soils under various loading conditions.\n\nBaziar et al. (2011) found that Ru-N/Nf data of sand-fine mixtures with FC = 60% significantly deviate from the data of clean sand, and thus extended the original model for soils with high fines contents.\n\nThe search results indicate that modern research has moved beyond simple intensity measures like PGA to more sophisticated correlations like cutoff CAV, which better capture the dynamic characteristics affecting pore pressure generation in sandy soils.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d52a3ef-833c-4d3d-a19f-380d6d5297be","uuid":"21267f30-55e8-4fbe-8f64-407b121942b9","timestamp":"2026-07-06T17:11:48.695Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CAV pore water pressure sandy soil correlation intensity measure Baziar Shahnazari","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01BuU4Yz8YeJkGp6C8wcQE3r","content":[{"title":"Correlations between Pore Pressure Development in Sandy Soil and 62 Ground Motion Intensity Measures by Chi-Chin Tsai, Jui-Pin Wang, Tsai-Yu Huang, Chia-Ying Sung :: SSRN","url":"https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4010372"},{"title":"Correlations between pore water pressure development in sandy soil and CAV-based ground motion intensity measures - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0013795222002708"},{"title":"Key factors affecting prediction of seismic pore water pressures in silty sands based on damage parameter | Bulletin of Earthquake Engineering | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10518-018-0411-z"},{"title":"A simple procedure to calibrate a pore pressure energy-based model from in situ tests | Acta Geotechnica | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11440-022-01650-1"},{"title":"Seismic Sliding Analysis of Sandy Slopes Subjected to Pore-Water Pressure Buildup | International Journal of Geomechanics | Vol 17, No 11","url":"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/abs/10.1061/(ASCE)GM.1943-5622.0001013"},{"title":"Stress-based evaluation of pore pressure generation in sands subjected to undrained cyclic loading - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1674775526001599"},{"title":"Excess pore water pressure generation in saturated sandy soils subjected to various cyclic stress paths - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0267726123000490"},{"title":"Prediction of Excess Pore Water Pressure Generation in Sand–Silt Mixtures During Cyclic Loading: A Dissipated Energy-Based Model | Geotechnical and Geological Engineering | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10706-024-02837-x"},{"title":"Pore Water Pressure Generation and Energy Dissipation Characteristics of Sand–Gravel Mixtures Subjected to Cyclic Loading","url":"https://www.mdpi.com/2673-7094/4/4/65"},{"title":"Rapid consolidation and compaction method for soil improvement of various layers of soils and intermediate geomaterials in a soil deposit","url":"https://image-ppubs.uspto.gov/dirsearch-public/print/downloadPdf/11124937"}]},"The search has returned relevant results focusing on the correlation between pore water pressure (PWP) development in sandy soils and various ground motion intensity measures, including CAV (cumulative absolute velocity).\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**CAV and Pore Water Pressure Correlation:**\nCutoff cumulative absolute velocities (CAV) with cutoff acceleration of 0.02~0.04 g are well correlated with PWP development in sandy soil, better than the original CAV without cutoff acceleration. PGA has a weak correlation with PWP development among the 62 intensity measures investigated, ranked 61st.\n\n**Baziar and Shahnazari's Research:**\nBaziar and Shahnazari conducted a laboratory study on the pore pressure generation model for Firouzkooh silty sands using hollow torsional test. Their research has focused on pore pressure generation in sandy and silty soils under various loading conditions.\n\nBaziar et al. (2011) found that Ru-N/Nf data of sand-fine mixtures with FC = 60% significantly deviate from the data of clean sand, and thus extended the original model for soils with high fines contents.\n\nThe search results indicate that modern research has moved beyond simple intensity measures like PGA to more sophisticated correlations like cutoff CAV, which better capture the dynamic characteristics affecting pore pressure generation in sandy soils."],"durationSeconds":11.991861208999994,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JKKhCL5xffqTx98F97W6Pw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Dobry threshold shear strain pore pressure generation cyclic 1982\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Pore Pressure Generation of Silty Sands due to Induced Cyclic Shear Strains | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/245295216_Pore_Pressure_Generation_of_Silty_Sands_due_to_Induced_Cyclic_Shear_Strains\"},{\"title\":\"Cyclic threshold shear strain in pore water pressure generation in clay in situ samples - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0038080618300684\"},{\"title\":\"Threshold Shear Strain for Cyclic Pore-Water Pressure in Cohesive Soils | Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering | Vol 132, No 10\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/%28ASCE%291090-0241%282006%29132%3A10%281325%29\"},{\"title\":\"Cyclic threshold shear strain for pore water pressure generation ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/journal/Frontiers-in-Marine-Science-2296-7745/publication/381611117_Cyclic_threshold_shear_strain_for_pore_water_pressure_generation_and_stiffness_degradation_in_marine_clays_at_Yangtze_estuary/links/667b5f72d21e220d89d2f720/Cyclic-threshold-shear-strain-for-pore-water-pressure-generation-and-stiffness-degradation-in-marine-clays-at-Yangtze-estuary.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Cyclic Pore Water Pressure Generation and Stiffness Degradation in Compacted Clays\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/281805790_Cyclic_Pore_Water_Pressure_Generation_and_Stiffness_Degradation_in_Compacted_Clays\"},{\"title\":\"Excess Pore Pressure Generation and Liquefaction of Gravelly Soil\",\"url\":\"https://par.nsf.gov/servlets/purl/10640728\"},{\"title\":\"Cyclic Threshold Shear Strains in Soils | Journal of Geotechnical Engineering | Vol 120, No 12\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/%28ASCE%290733-9410%281994%29120%3A12%282208%29\"},{\"title\":\"Frontiers | Cyclic threshold shear strain for pore water pressure generation and stiffness degradation in marine clays at Yangtze estuary\",\"url\":\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2023.1184225/full\"},{\"title\":\"Cyclic Shear Strain Needed for Liquefaction Triggering and ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Ricardo-Dobry/publication/279239866_Cyclic_Shear_Strain_Needed_for_Liquefaction_Triggering_and_Assessment_of_Overburden_Pressure_Factor_Ks/links/559a8f5d08ae5d8f3937dbc3/Cyclic-Shear-Strain-Needed-for-Liquefaction-Triggering-and-Assessment-of-Overburden-Pressure-Factor-Ks.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Stress-based evaluation of pore pressure generation in sands subjected to undrained cyclic loading - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1674775526001599\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about the Dobry et al. 1982 work on threshold shear strain and pore pressure generation:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nDobry et al. (1982) first proposed a shear-strain-based framework to analyze the generation of excess porewater pressure as well as liquefaction.\n\nThe specific publication was \"Prediction of pore-water pressure buildup and liquefaction of sands during earthquakes by the cyclic strain method,\" published in the National Bureau of Standards Building Science Series No. 138 in July 1982.\n\n## Threshold Shear Strain Concept\n\nThreshold shear strain for cyclic pore-water pressure, γt, is a fundamental property of fully saturated soils subjected to undrained cyclic loading. When the cyclic shear strain amplitude (γc) is below the threshold, negligible pore water pressure is generated, and when γc exceeds the threshold, pore water pressure accumulates significantly.\n\n## Impact and Legacy\n\nMany experimental studies have been performed on threshold shear strain values of saturated sands following Dobry et al. (1982), using various testing methods including cyclic triaxial tests, cyclic hollow cylinder torsional shear tests, and cyclic direct simple shear tests. The Dobry et al. 1982 work is recognized as a foundational strain-based model for characterizing residual excess pore water pressure generation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d52a3ef-833c-4d3d-a19f-380d6d5297be","uuid":"8caa1b7b-e608-49eb-b76f-1a8af95fee31","timestamp":"2026-07-06T17:11:52.089Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Dobry threshold shear strain pore pressure generation cyclic 1982","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01NtGWfhYhyrJ3usn4pGriZy","content":[{"title":"Pore Pressure Generation of Silty Sands due to Induced Cyclic Shear Strains | Request PDF","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/245295216_Pore_Pressure_Generation_of_Silty_Sands_due_to_Induced_Cyclic_Shear_Strains"},{"title":"Cyclic threshold shear strain in pore water pressure generation in clay in situ samples - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0038080618300684"},{"title":"Threshold Shear Strain for Cyclic Pore-Water Pressure in Cohesive Soils | Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering | Vol 132, No 10","url":"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/%28ASCE%291090-0241%282006%29132%3A10%281325%29"},{"title":"Cyclic threshold shear strain for pore water pressure generation ...","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/journal/Frontiers-in-Marine-Science-2296-7745/publication/381611117_Cyclic_threshold_shear_strain_for_pore_water_pressure_generation_and_stiffness_degradation_in_marine_clays_at_Yangtze_estuary/links/667b5f72d21e220d89d2f720/Cyclic-threshold-shear-strain-for-pore-water-pressure-generation-and-stiffness-degradation-in-marine-clays-at-Yangtze-estuary.pdf"},{"title":"(PDF) Cyclic Pore Water Pressure Generation and Stiffness Degradation in Compacted Clays","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/281805790_Cyclic_Pore_Water_Pressure_Generation_and_Stiffness_Degradation_in_Compacted_Clays"},{"title":"Excess Pore Pressure Generation and Liquefaction of Gravelly Soil","url":"https://par.nsf.gov/servlets/purl/10640728"},{"title":"Cyclic Threshold Shear Strains in Soils | Journal of Geotechnical Engineering | Vol 120, No 12","url":"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/%28ASCE%290733-9410%281994%29120%3A12%282208%29"},{"title":"Frontiers | Cyclic threshold shear strain for pore water pressure generation and stiffness degradation in marine clays at Yangtze estuary","url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2023.1184225/full"},{"title":"Cyclic Shear Strain Needed for Liquefaction Triggering and ...","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Ricardo-Dobry/publication/279239866_Cyclic_Shear_Strain_Needed_for_Liquefaction_Triggering_and_Assessment_of_Overburden_Pressure_Factor_Ks/links/559a8f5d08ae5d8f3937dbc3/Cyclic-Shear-Strain-Needed-for-Liquefaction-Triggering-and-Assessment-of-Overburden-Pressure-Factor-Ks.pdf"},{"title":"Stress-based evaluation of pore pressure generation in sands subjected to undrained cyclic loading - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1674775526001599"}]},"Based on the search results, I found comprehensive information about the Dobry et al. 1982 work on threshold shear strain and pore pressure generation:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nDobry et al. (1982) first proposed a shear-strain-based framework to analyze the generation of excess porewater pressure as well as liquefaction.\n\nThe specific publication was \"Prediction of pore-water pressure buildup and liquefaction of sands during earthquakes by the cyclic strain method,\" published in the National Bureau of Standards Building Science Series No. 138 in July 1982.\n\n## Threshold Shear Strain Concept\n\nThreshold shear strain for cyclic pore-water pressure, γt, is a fundamental property of fully saturated soils subjected to undrained cyclic loading. When the cyclic shear strain amplitude (γc) is below the threshold, negligible pore water pressure is generated, and when γc exceeds the threshold, pore water pressure accumulates significantly.\n\n## Impact and Legacy\n\nMany experimental studies have been performed on threshold shear strain values of saturated sands following Dobry et al. (1982), using various testing methods including cyclic triaxial tests, cyclic hollow cylinder torsional shear tests, and cyclic direct simple shear tests. The Dobry et al. 1982 work is recognized as a foundational strain-based model for characterizing residual excess pore water pressure generation."],"durationSeconds":14.297797374999995,"searchCount":1}}
