{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QWwAUF2tgsQAQn6f59rdff","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"screening seismic records tailings dams spectral power low frequency record selection arxiv 2020\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[2009.06426] Screening of seismic records to perform time-history dynamic analyses of tailings dams: a power-spectral based approach\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.06426\"},{\"title\":\"Screening of seismic records to perform time-history dynamic analyses of tailings dams: a power-spectral based approach - ADS\",\"url\":\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2020arXiv200906426L/abstract\"},{\"title\":\"Screening of seismic records to perform time-history dynamic analyses of tailings dams: A power-spectral based approach - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S026772612100172X\"},{\"title\":\"Screening of seismic records to perform time-history dynamic analyses of   tailings dams: a power-spectral based approach\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2009.06426\"},{\"title\":\"Seismic Performance of a Tailings Dam Located in Hight Seismicity Area | Bellido | ASEAN Journal of Science and Engineering\",\"url\":\"https://ejournal.upi.edu/index.php/AJSE/article/view/75557\"},{\"title\":\"Effect of embankment construction quality on stability of Aketao tailings dam under rainfall-seismic coupling | Journal of Mountain Science | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11629-024-9445-7\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] Screening of seismic records to perform time-history dynamic analyses of tailings dams: A power-spectral based approach | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Screening-of-seismic-records-to-perform-dynamic-of-Labanda-Sottile/3497b29cb08da1b9433f7eda1da621abddf1602f\"}]\n\nI found the research paper you're looking for! Here are the key details:\n\n**Title:** Screening of seismic records to perform time-history dynamic analyses of tailings dams: a power-spectral based approach\n\n**Authors:** Nicolás A. Labanda, Mauro G. Sottile, Ignacio A. Cueto, and Alejo O. Sfriso\n\n**Source:** The paper is available on arXiv (2009.06426) and was published in 2021 in Soil Dynamics and Earthquake Engineering.\n\n**Key Concept:** The procedure makes use of the spectral properties of the seismic record, considering only the intensity of the frequency content which is not filtered by the dam to obtain an a priori estimate of demand, expressed in terms of displacements.\n\n**Purpose:** An a priori simple tool is used to predict which seismic records would yield a given demand, thus obtaining estimations with much fewer runs. In order to perform a more precise selection, a semi-analytical screening procedure is presented.\n\nThe full paper is available at: https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.06426\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d52a3ef-833c-4d3d-a19f-380d6d5297be","uuid":"5e10c7d8-7bb9-4df2-9a7c-fb2a2a9ef853","timestamp":"2026-07-06T17:12:13.493Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"screening seismic records tailings dams spectral power low frequency record selection arxiv 2020","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01GWf5XeEfSFPKgaiXvnZPQn","content":[{"title":"[2009.06426] Screening of seismic records to perform time-history dynamic analyses of tailings dams: a power-spectral based approach","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.06426"},{"title":"Screening of seismic records to perform time-history dynamic analyses of tailings dams: a power-spectral based approach - ADS","url":"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2020arXiv200906426L/abstract"},{"title":"Screening of seismic records to perform time-history dynamic analyses of tailings dams: A power-spectral based approach - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S026772612100172X"},{"title":"Screening of seismic records to perform time-history dynamic analyses of   tailings dams: a power-spectral based approach","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2009.06426"},{"title":"Seismic Performance of a Tailings Dam Located in Hight Seismicity Area | Bellido | ASEAN Journal of Science and Engineering","url":"https://ejournal.upi.edu/index.php/AJSE/article/view/75557"},{"title":"Effect of embankment construction quality on stability of Aketao tailings dam under rainfall-seismic coupling | Journal of Mountain Science | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11629-024-9445-7"},{"title":"[PDF] Screening of seismic records to perform time-history dynamic analyses of tailings dams: A power-spectral based approach | Semantic Scholar","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Screening-of-seismic-records-to-perform-dynamic-of-Labanda-Sottile/3497b29cb08da1b9433f7eda1da621abddf1602f"}]},"I found the research paper you're looking for! Here are the key details:\n\n**Title:** Screening of seismic records to perform time-history dynamic analyses of tailings dams: a power-spectral based approach\n\n**Authors:** Nicolás A. Labanda, Mauro G. Sottile, Ignacio A. Cueto, and Alejo O. Sfriso\n\n**Source:** The paper is available on arXiv (2009.06426) and was published in 2021 in Soil Dynamics and Earthquake Engineering.\n\n**Key Concept:** The procedure makes use of the spectral properties of the seismic record, considering only the intensity of the frequency content which is not filtered by the dam to obtain an a priori estimate of demand, expressed in terms of displacements.\n\n**Purpose:** An a priori simple tool is used to predict which seismic records would yield a given demand, thus obtaining estimations with much fewer runs. In order to perform a more precise selection, a semi-analytical screening procedure is presented.\n\nThe full paper is available at: https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.06426"],"durationSeconds":7.709445915999997,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011erQsn8NRPjKFXhQLt245g","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"blast vibration PPV response spectra inadequate geotechnical tailings pore pressure cumulative damage\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"of blasting on pore pressure\",\"url\":\"https://files.dep.state.pa.us/Mining/BureauOfMiningPrograms/BMPPortalFiles/Blasting_Research_Papers/Slope%20Stability/BoR%20Blasting%20and%20dams.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Prediction of Blast-Induced Vibration Parameters for Soil Sites | International Journal of Geomechanics | Vol 14, No 3\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/abs/10.1061/(ASCE)GM.1943-5622.0000355\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Determination of blast induced ground vibration equations for rocks using mechanical and geological properties\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/298484361_Determination_of_blast_induced_ground_vibration_equations_for_rocks_using_mechanical_and_geological_properties\"},{\"title\":\"Accurate prediction of blast-induced ground vibration intensity using optimized machine learning models - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2214914725002028\"},{\"title\":\"Ground Vibrations and Air Blast Effects Induced by Blasting in Op\",\"url\":\"https://www.longdom.org/open-access/ground-vibrations-and-air-blast-effects-induced-by-blasting-in-open-pit-mines-case-of-metlaoui-mining-basin-southwestern-40660.html\"},{\"title\":\"Determination of blast-induced ground vibration equations for rocks using mechanical and geological properties - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S167477551600024X\"},{\"title\":\"Vibration velocity and frequency characteristics of surrounding rock of adjacent tunnel under blasting excavation\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9120496/\"},{\"title\":\"Frontiers | Experimental Study on the Evolution of Dynamic Pore Pressure and Unidirectional and Bidirectional Vibrations of Phosphogypsum\",\"url\":\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/earth-science/articles/10.3389/feart.2022.929777/full\"},{\"title\":\"Determination of Blast Vibration Safety Criteria for Buried Polyethylene Pipelines Adjacent to Blast Areas, Using Vibration Velocity and Strain Data\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10384277/\"},{\"title\":\"Propagation and Prediction of Blasting Vibration on Ground Surface Induced by Underground Mining with Comparison to Vibration Inside Rock | Rock Mechanics and Rock Engineering | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00603-024-03985-5\"}]\n\nI've performed the web search for your query on blast vibration PPV response spectra in relation to geotechnical tailings, pore pressure, and cumulative damage. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Blast-Induced Vibration and Pore Pressure in Tailings\n\nResearch by Obermeyer measured no significant increase in residual pore-water pressures in a hydraulic fill uranium tailings dam subjected to blast-induced vibrations with particle velocities as high as 2 cm/s. However, significant blast-induced residual pore-water pressure increases have been reported in saturated, loose cohesionless deposits by other researchers.\n\n## PPV Parameters and Empirical Models\n\nSite-specific empirical models for blast-induced vibration parameters like peak particle velocity (PPV), peak pressure (PP), peak particle displacement (PPD), and pore pressure ratio (PPR) are commonly used for blast-resistant designs. However, these empirical models do not consider the variation in soil properties, such as the degree of saturation and uncertain in situ conditions.\n\n## Response Spectra Analysis\n\nDue to traditional inadequate prediction methods, response spectral analysis and normalized pseudo velocity response spectra (NPVRS) are employed to create a novel approach for illustrating ground motions.\n\n## Key Concerns\n\nIncreased pore-water pressures cause the shear strength of a soil to decrease. The major concern is the potential for blast-induced residual pore-water pressure increases that reduce the shear strength of a soil long enough to allow gravity to cause the failure of the slopes of earth structures.\n\nThe search results indicate that while PPV-based methods exist, there are recognized limitations in traditional prediction approaches for blast-induced effects on geotechnical structures like tailings dams.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d52a3ef-833c-4d3d-a19f-380d6d5297be","uuid":"aedf6ad0-7138-4c1a-ac87-ed37e56d5008","timestamp":"2026-07-06T17:12:17.352Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"blast vibration PPV response spectra inadequate geotechnical tailings pore pressure cumulative damage","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01MSL8pWxei9t17WoMcuaxEL","content":[{"title":"of blasting on pore pressure","url":"https://files.dep.state.pa.us/Mining/BureauOfMiningPrograms/BMPPortalFiles/Blasting_Research_Papers/Slope%20Stability/BoR%20Blasting%20and%20dams.pdf"},{"title":"Prediction of Blast-Induced Vibration Parameters for Soil Sites | International Journal of Geomechanics | Vol 14, No 3","url":"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/abs/10.1061/(ASCE)GM.1943-5622.0000355"},{"title":"(PDF) Determination of blast induced ground vibration equations for rocks using mechanical and geological properties","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/298484361_Determination_of_blast_induced_ground_vibration_equations_for_rocks_using_mechanical_and_geological_properties"},{"title":"Accurate prediction of blast-induced ground vibration intensity using optimized machine learning models - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2214914725002028"},{"title":"Ground Vibrations and Air Blast Effects Induced by Blasting in Op","url":"https://www.longdom.org/open-access/ground-vibrations-and-air-blast-effects-induced-by-blasting-in-open-pit-mines-case-of-metlaoui-mining-basin-southwestern-40660.html"},{"title":"Determination of blast-induced ground vibration equations for rocks using mechanical and geological properties - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S167477551600024X"},{"title":"Vibration velocity and frequency characteristics of surrounding rock of adjacent tunnel under blasting excavation","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9120496/"},{"title":"Frontiers | Experimental Study on the Evolution of Dynamic Pore Pressure and Unidirectional and Bidirectional Vibrations of Phosphogypsum","url":"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/earth-science/articles/10.3389/feart.2022.929777/full"},{"title":"Determination of Blast Vibration Safety Criteria for Buried Polyethylene Pipelines Adjacent to Blast Areas, Using Vibration Velocity and Strain Data","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10384277/"},{"title":"Propagation and Prediction of Blasting Vibration on Ground Surface Induced by Underground Mining with Comparison to Vibration Inside Rock | Rock Mechanics and Rock Engineering | Springer Nature Link","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00603-024-03985-5"}]},"I've performed the web search for your query on blast vibration PPV response spectra in relation to geotechnical tailings, pore pressure, and cumulative damage. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Blast-Induced Vibration and Pore Pressure in Tailings\n\nResearch by Obermeyer measured no significant increase in residual pore-water pressures in a hydraulic fill uranium tailings dam subjected to blast-induced vibrations with particle velocities as high as 2 cm/s. However, significant blast-induced residual pore-water pressure increases have been reported in saturated, loose cohesionless deposits by other researchers.\n\n## PPV Parameters and Empirical Models\n\nSite-specific empirical models for blast-induced vibration parameters like peak particle velocity (PPV), peak pressure (PP), peak particle displacement (PPD), and pore pressure ratio (PPR) are commonly used for blast-resistant designs. However, these empirical models do not consider the variation in soil properties, such as the degree of saturation and uncertain in situ conditions.\n\n## Response Spectra Analysis\n\nDue to traditional inadequate prediction methods, response spectral analysis and normalized pseudo velocity response spectra (NPVRS) are employed to create a novel approach for illustrating ground motions.\n\n## Key Concerns\n\nIncreased pore-water pressures cause the shear strength of a soil to decrease. The major concern is the potential for blast-induced residual pore-water pressure increases that reduce the shear strength of a soil long enough to allow gravity to cause the failure of the slopes of earth structures.\n\nThe search results indicate that while PPV-based methods exist, there are recognized limitations in traditional prediction approaches for blast-induced effects on geotechnical structures like tailings dams."],"durationSeconds":11.557113708000019,"searchCount":1}}
